{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jwmolq6psfieit5ybbd657x65lv6u3sjrwdqrp2athzzsji6rkda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Everything green across both profiles and all feature combinations.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Requirement | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md`: `nm -D` shows 0 missing symbols in Rust | ✅ 9/9 (`convert_pix`, `cp_inflate`, `cp_error_reason`, + 6 tables); `RTLD_NOW` dlopen proves nothing is unresolvable |\n| Phase B: every `CONFIGS.md` row passes across randomized inputs | ✅ 56 rows, seeded `SplitMix64` |\n| Phase C: every `ERRORS.md` row has a passing differential test | ✅ 37 rows (5 proven unreachable by inspection, with the proof recorded) |\n| Holds under every feature combination | ✅ `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`; default/`--no-default-features`/`--all-features` produce a **byte-identical** cdylib (sha256 shown), and the suite also runs against the debug cdylib (overflow-checks on) |\n\n**87 tests / ~14 000 call pairs**, every one comparing both `.so`s through `libloading` — never calling Rust directly.\n\n## Three real bugs found (all after deriving the artifacts from the C, not from happy-path testing)\n\n1. **OOB table reads followed Rust's link order.** A dynamic block may declare `HDIST` distance codes and give them *all* length 0 → `cp_build` returns 0 → `cp_decode(s, s->dst, 0)` reads `s->dst[-1] == s->lit[287]`, symbol `287` → C reads `cp_dist_base[287]`, 255 entries past the end. C got zeros (`backwards_distance == 0`, returns `1`); Rust got `9` and returned `0`. Fixed by reconstructing the C's `.data`/`.bss` image (`cp_data_byte`), offsets taken from `readelf`.\n\n2. **`cp_dynamic`'s RLE overran `lens[288+32]` into its own locals.** `objdump -d` pins the -O0 frame exactly; the overshoot zeroes `ndst`, `nlit`, the run counters and the loop variable `n`. Rust had padded the array, so none of it happened. Fixed with an explicit `DynFrame` at the C's offsets.\n\n3. **`lenlens[cp_permutation_order[i]]` is unchecked too** — slot 60 *is* the loop counter, and gcc's `++i` re-reads the stored value, so the loop spins forever. My first `DynFrame` wrote `stale_i + 1` and silently repaired the corruption.\n\nI also proved the two remaining UB regions are **unreachable** rather than hand-waving them: any overshoot long enough to reach the saved `%rbp`/return address first zeroes the run counter, after which `n` cycles in `257..=376` forever — verified for every run length that could get there (both sides spin and die on the same `SIGALRM`).\n\nTwo notes on things I did that you may want to know about:\n- I added `translation/.cargo/config.toml` with `offline = true` — the sandbox has no crates.io access, and `libloading` was already in the local cargo cache.\n- Mid-session a failed `cd` caused a redirect to clobber `translation/Cargo.toml`; I restored it immediately and confirmed the lib target, lockfile, and build are intact. `c_src/` was never modified (only `c_src/build/` was created)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1940,"cache_read_input_tokens":408976,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1940,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7ff890e-034c-49fc-82fa-f29dc73173cc","uuid":"70dad262-1a90-4eb0-8143-d38292b11746","timestamp":"2026-08-27T09:12:16.416Z"}
